 "title": "A dag-like Res(xor) bound for bit LeftPigeon reduces to hole-row separation",
 "subject": "The binary left-pigeon principle, PPADS-complete, in resolution over parities",
 "conclusion": "Braun's generic Res(xor) criterion applies to the binary left-pigeon principle with its own clauses, so a superpolynomial dag-like Res(xor) lower bound for this PPADS-complete principle follows from one statement: its row-linear polynomials over pigeon and hole rows stay separated from the polynomial calculus's consequences at degree about 12 k log n for some k = omega(sqrt(n log n)).",
